## Lore

The Feni come from Fen, a violently unstable world whose climate can swing
to extremes within a single generation. Every living thing there evolved to
cope with constant change, and the Feni most of all: their bodies reshape
themselves to suit almost any environment. With no stable land to build on,
they never settled into towns; they are wanderers who keep their history in
stories and songs, and had no word for city before they reached Earth.

On Rifts Earth they look vaguely like deer: sleek and furred, with long
necks, thin graceful limbs, doglegged hind legs ending in three-toed hooves,
and oddly human arms ending in three horn-covered fingers and a thumb. They
walk upright but can run on all fours, and their hands handle weapons, armor
and gadgets as well as anyone''s.

Feni are jumpy creatures ruled by fight or flight. Their first instinct is
to run and live another day, which earns them a name for cowardice. Corner
one, or threaten its mate or young, and it flips into a terrifying berserker
rage, aiming to cripple or drive off the threat as fast as possible so the
others can escape. That protective drive extends to the children and women
of any race; many tales tell of Feni appearing out of the woods to rescue a
child.

For all their skittishness they are curious, love to explore and are
always on the move, following a seasonal migration across the wilds of
North America.

## GM Notes

Also known as Deerstalkers and Demon Fawn. Size 4 to 4.6 feet (1.2 to 1.4 m)
at the shoulder, 5.6 to 7 feet (1.7 to 2.1 m) overall with neck and head.
Weight 130 to 200 pounds (58.5 to 90 kg). Life span 2D6+33 years; mature at
10; one or two young after a 7 month gestation, as often as every two years
up to age 32.

Travel in family clans of 6D6 or herd-like tribes of 3D4x100, migrating
south and west in winter and north and east in summer; most common in the
Pacific Northwest, Northern Mexico, Canada and the West Coast. Prefer heavily
wooded temperate regions and love fresh snow.

Disposition: skittish with strangers, especially groups of more than 8 and
urban settings; loyal but jumpy even with friends; good-natured and kind.

Slave market value 1D4x1,000 with low demand; the Splugorth buy them as prey
for the Atlantis game preserves. Some barbarians and D-Bees pay 1D4x100 to
eat them.

Allies: gentle peoples such as the Amana, Sasquatch, Cactus People and
Fennodi; sometimes Native Americans, Blucies, Elemental Fusionists, Druids
and adventurer groups, where they serve as scouts. Enemies: Psi-Stalkers,
barbarians, slavers, Dark Hounds, Mystic Knights, Worm Wraiths,
Oborus-Slitherers and Devil Unicorns hunt them; they fear the Minions of
Splugorth, Horune Pirates and Coalition soldiers. Simvan scorn them but
mostly leave them alone.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'feni-nomad');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'feni-nomad';

